## The full handoff bundle

Everything you need lives in **`.handoff/`**:

| File | What's in it |
|------|--------------|
| `project-brief.md` | What the project is: purpose, architecture, mental model |
| `state-of-play.md` | Works / in-progress / blocked / half-done |
| `decision-log.md` | **Why** key decisions were made |
| `gotchas.md` | Traps, fragile zones, "don't touch" |
| `environment.md` | What you must set up: runtime, deps, MCP, secrets (by name), services |
| `onboarding-protocol.md` | The guided-transition plan |
| `known-unknowns.md` | What even the previous owner was unsure about |
| `manifest.yaml` | Bundle metadata + freshness stamp |

Claims are tagged `[declared]` (the previous owner said so), `[inferred]` (deduced from
the code/history — may be wrong), or `[uncertain]` (flagged as unsure).

## Two ways to onboard

- **If you have the `claude-to-claude` skill:** run **`/claude-to-claude onboard`** — your Claude will verify the
  bundle, help you reconstruct the environment with smoke tests, give a calibrated tour,
  propose a safe first task, and archive this scaffolding when you've settled in.
- **If you don't:** ask your Claude to *read `.handoff/` and walk you through it*. That's
  enough to get a coherent guided readout.

